/// Allocates past a single arena chunk, on purpose.
///
/// The canary for leakcheck.sh.  Every ctest program fits inside one 1 MB
/// chunk, and one chunk is still reachable through the allocator's own bump
/// pointer -- so none of them leaks even with the exit handler removed, and a
/// leak check built only from them would pass forever without testing
/// anything.  This one abandons chunks, which is the case that actually goes
/// wrong.
///
/// Verified both ways, against the runtime as it was before the chunk list
/// existed: 20 leaks and 21 MB at this size, and none once the chunks are
/// tracked and freed.
///
/// ⚠️ Disabling only the atexit handler does NOT reproduce the old bug -- the
/// chunk list itself keeps every chunk reachable, so `leaks` reports nothing.
/// Reproducing it means going back to the untracked allocator.
begin
    var Text := '';
    for var I := 0; I < 1000; I := I + 1 do
        Text := Text + 'padding padding padding padding padding ';

    WriteLn(Length(Text));
end
